{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789247615,"nonce":"qM0rKXwcTYbcuxQ8JJN7hkwsFXI=","title":"Core collections must stop a hosted wren_lift thread","message":"A wren_lift VM hosted by caribou-wren does not register its thread as a\ncore mutator: if it did, the core's trigger could fire inside allocate and\nreset the shared trigger before wren_lift's own cycle runs. Consequence:\na core collection started from another runtime's thread does not stop\nthe wren_lift thread. The heap record is safe (it is only touched under\nthe GC lock) but a precise trace of an object mid-write is not.\n\nFine for a process with only wren_lift on the core. Before a second\nresident shares a world with it, either the adapter drives wren_lift's\ntrigger from the core's (so the thread can register as a mutator and\nreach safepoints) or wren_lift's allocation slow path becomes a\nsafepoint. Related: should_collect() has no heartbeat, so idle wren_lift\ngarbage is never collected under a host (wren_lift's own heap collects\nevery 30 s).","files":null}]}